  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSERVATION OF CHIMPANZEES IN SOUTHERN TANGANYIKA ECOSYSTEM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO SECURE THE LONG-TERM PROTECTION OF CHIMPANZEES IN TANZANIAS SOUTH TANGANYIKA REGION BY INCREASING UNDERSTANDING OF CHIMPANZEE POPULATION STATUS AND GEOGRAPHICAL DISTRIBUTION, AND REDUCING CHIMPANZEE HABITAT LOSS. ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: 1) UPDATING THE CHIMPANZEE POPULATION ESTIMATE FOR THE REGION 2) MAPPING CHIMPANZEE DISTRIBUTION 3) DETERMINING THE CURRENT CONDITION OF CHIMPANZEE HABITATS 4) SUPPORTING PATROLS BY TANZANIA FOREST SERVICES, TANZANIA WILDLIFE AUTHORITY, AND LOCAL GOVERNMENT AUTHORITIES TO ENSURE WILDLIFE CONSERVATION 5) ESTABLISHING LAND-USE PLANS IN TWO VILLAGES THAT POSE A HIGH THREAT TO CHIMPANZEES 6) CONDUCTING STAKEHOLDER WORKSHOPS ON THE ECOLOGICAL IMPORTANCE OF CHIMPANZEES AND 7) RAISING COMMUNITY AWARENESS OF THE CONSERVATION VALUE OF CHIMPANZEES.</narrative>
  </description>
